@title 3D: heat and EMC switch off from the toolbar and stay off, one switch each
@area 3D
@sizes 1366x768 1920x1080
# The 3D toolbar's Heat and EMC are the only switches of those views: Heat off takes the strip, a finished result with its overlay and legend, and both panels with it; EMC off takes its panel and legend; neither comes back by itself. The Layers list reads in full (docs/design/3d-panels-audit.md).
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-cooling-advice.novo
wait 20
click_text 3D #1
wait 30
shot 3d-start
click_text Heat #1
wait 5
# Heat starts a run by itself on a small cabinet (as in scenario 135): switch Auto off first so no run restarts, then stop the running one, else Quality and Simulate stay greyed.
click_text Auto #1
wait 10
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 30
try click_text Cancel
wait 20
expect "Vents and fans"
shot heat-on
click_text "Settings for the next run"
wait 10
try click_text Quick
wait 10
click_text Simulate #2
wait_s 100
wait 60
wait_s 100
wait 60
expect "Heat: "
shot heat-result
check_layout
click 24 428
wait 20
expect_not "Air speed"
expect_not "Vents and fans"
shot heat-off
click 24 464
wait 30
expect "Indicative model"
shot emc-on
click 24 464
wait 30
expect_not "Indicative model"
shot emc-off
wait 30
expect_not "Indicative model"
check_layout
click_text Layers #1
wait 20
expect "Walk through"
expect "Slotted ducts"
expect "Connection points"
expect "Missing part data"
shot layers
check_layout
move 65 420
wait 40
shot layers-occlusion-hint
